M0 ABI test

  ./gen_abi.py [--linux DIR] [--sysroot DIR] [--keep]

Checks that every VIDIOC_* / MEDIA_* ioctl in videodev2.h, media.h and
v4l2-subdev.h has the same direction, group, number and argument size on
FreeBSD (clang, aarch64, FreeBSD sysroot, <sys/ioccom.h>) as in the Linux UAPI
(reference tree: /opt/bzdos/linux-work/linux-6.12). The Linux table is
computed twice, natively and as an aarch64 object read back from .rodata, and
both must agree. The raw ioctl numbers differ between the systems (direction
bits are swapped and the size field is 13 bits against 14), so numbers are
never compared directly.

The FreeBSD side takes videodev2.h, v4l2-controls.h and v4l2-common.h from
../../uapi, and the GPL-only headers from the Linux tree.

shim/              what <linux/...> resolves to on the FreeBSD side
linux-asm-shim/    asm/ and kernel-internal headers the Linux UAPI expects
linux-a64-shim/    sys/time.h for the bare aarch64-linux-gnu cross compiler
